lly through his sons Hasan and Husayn.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/alien-act-1705"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alien-act-1705.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Alien Act 1705</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Alien Act 1705 was a law of the English Parliament designed to force Scotland into negotiations for union.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/alikhan-bukeikhanov"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alikhan-bukeikhanov.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Alikhan Bukeikhanov</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Alikhan Bukeikhanov was a Kazakh scholar and politician, a descendant of Genghis Khan through the Kazakh khans, and a member of the Russian Kadet party.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/alim-khan-of-kokand"><span class="enc-name">Alim Khan of Kokand</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Alim Khan was a ruler of the Ming dynasty of Kokand who took the title khan around 1800, turning the Kokand state into a khanate.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/alimirah-hanfare"><span class="enc-name">Alimirah Hanfare</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Alimirah Hanfare was Sultan of Aussa, the traditional leader of the Afar people of Ethiopia, from 1944 until his death in 2011.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/alimuly"><span class="enc-name">Alimuly</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Alimuly are one of the three main tribal groupings of the Junior Zhuz, the western branch of the Kazakh people, made up of six clans.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/alise-sainte-reine"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/image